96
00:05:57,593 --> 00:05:59,253
Make sure it all has the same radius.

97
00:05:59,253 --> 00:06:00,633
And then this is where the calculus comes in.

98
00:06:00,713 --> 00:06:04,013
If you look at tangent lines, you know what tangent lines are, I hope.

99
00:06:04,713 --> 00:06:05,673
You probably don't.

100
00:06:06,433 --> 00:06:09,853
But the slope of the tangent line is sort of the slope of,

101
00:06:09,933 --> 00:06:14,473
if you were to draw the slope through the grid squares of the circle,

102
00:06:14,933 --> 00:06:16,733
this made a lot more sense inside my head.

103
00:06:16,733 --> 00:06:22,553
But you can trace pretty much any circle on the graph paper and repeat this process.

104
00:06:22,673 --> 00:06:26,073
Just make sure the radius is the same and that each quadrant is the same.

105
00:06:26,173 --> 00:06:28,153
And there you go, you have a circle in Minecraft.

